{"id": "EUVD-2026-108311", "enisaUuid": "7cb69f69-91d4-30fe-bf6e-11cd19f8c451", "description": "Wasmtime 39.0.0 before 48.0.4 and 49.0.0 before 49.0.2 contains a stack buffer overflow vulnerability that allows malicious guests to write ~16KB to the native stack via unvalidated async callback result types. Attackers can supply components with mistyped component-model-async callback functions to overwrite return addresses, crashing the host or escaping the sandbox.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:51", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-32h6-97mm-8q3c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-39.0.0-before-48.0.4-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.2-stack-buffer-overflow"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115384", "GHSA-6fff-wrjr-wjxr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "715016b2-b555-3042-b16b-30e41774069f", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.2"}, {"id": "c1f2da0a-8377-3f31-a5fd-6ff61b020054", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "39.0.0 <48.0.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "228708a4-2b19-31c9-b6ab-a66a96e067fd", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}